# Environment
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Generated data — reproducible from the seeded generator, not committed.
# Test fixtures are exempt: they're small, hand-written, and part of the
# suite's meaning, so a blanket *.csv would silently drop them.
*.csv
!tests/fixtures/*.csv

# Trained model artifacts — reproducible via ml/train.py, EXCEPT the
# versions pinned below: main.py::boot_version() loads an artifact at import
# time (boot-time, not per-request), so Render needs a real model on disk the
# moment it clones this repo, and training data (*.csv, also gitignored
# above) isn't committed for it to retrain from on deploy.
#
# Pin BOTH the version the shared registry currently calls live AND any newer
# candidate you want promotable from a fresh instance. boot_version() only
# honours the registry's answer when that version is `in on_disk`; if the
# registry's choice isn't pinned here, a freshly cloned instance silently
# falls back to "newest on disk" and auto-promotes — which this project
# treats as a human decision, never a side effect of a restart.
#
# 2026-08-06-055755 — pre-crop-expansion (9-crop encoder vocabulary), what
#   the registry currently marks current.
# 2026-08-19-160748 — retrained against the 35-crop vocabulary (Task 9 of
#   docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-18-crop-coverage-expansion.md); on disk and
#   promotable, but not live until a human promotes it.
#
# If you retrain and want the new version deployed, add its pinned path here,
# commit the new (small) artifact directory, and promote it explicitly.
ml/artifacts/*
!ml/artifacts/2026-08-06-055755/
!ml/artifacts/2026-08-06-055755/**
!ml/artifacts/2026-08-19-160748/
!ml/artifacts/2026-08-19-160748/**

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
